     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. The total area of APL (Land allocated for any non-forest purpose (also known as non-forest area)) forest under enhanced protection in the 3 provinces, namely East Kalimantan, Central Kalimantan and Wes Kalimantan is 663.777 ha, surpassing the end-target of 500.000 ha by nearly 30 percent.
2. UNDP helped the provincial government in East Kalimantan, Central Kalimantan and West Kalimantan through data analysis, expert and multistakeholder discussions, to draft to 11 national or provincial instruction or decrees supporting the conversation of APL (Land allocated for any non-forest purpose (also known as non-forest area)), and in which bioiversity and ecosystem services have been mainstreamed to an extent. These regulations has impacted to 33,58 mTons CO2eq have been avoided based at district level. This figure represents 33.58 mTons CO2eq from avoided deforestation (92,580 ha). 
3. Partnerships, UNDP&#x2019;s engagement of stakeholders in Forest Area Planning &amp; Management in Kalimanta has been strong, and it has in fact been a key part of UNDP&#x2019;s approach in its work at the provincial and district levels. It has aimed to adapt to local government preferences regarding APL forest management to identify conservation opportunities and have subnational officials take ownership of the achievements. For every regulation drafted with technical support from UNDP, there were several consultations with stakeholders conducted through the process to gain the greatest consensus possible.</narrative>
